OL,3,GNEWSAHave you seen the hummingbird hawk
OL,4,Amoth?
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs parts of the West Midlands baked in
OL,7,Fwarmer temperatures this summer,
OL,8,Fspecies once considered unusual in the
OL,9,Fregion, such as hummingbird hawk moths,
OL,10,Fivy bees and the wasp spider have been
OL,11,Fspotted in growing numbers.
OL,13,FThe hummingbird hawk moth, known for
OL,14,Fits furry grey body, orange hindwings
OL,15,Fand long proboscis, migrates to the UK
OL,16,Ffrom southern Europe and north Africa
OL,17,Fin the summer months.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
